# Default-deny build context: the image ships only what the web app needs to
# run. Everything else -- git history, the venv, local data and plan docs,
# .scratch/, editor and tooling state -- stays out without having to be named.
# A new top-level path the image needs means adding a `!` line below.
*
**

!src/
!web_main.py
!pyproject.toml
!poetry.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!docker/

# Re-exclude what the web image must not carry inside the allowed trees. The
# desktop UI imports PyQt6; leaving it out proves nothing else needs it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
src/ui/
